@host = http://localhost:5235

### Every call below is also upserted into classified_queries (the query
### log): the embedding is written once, times_classified and the best
### candidate refresh on every repeat. A query that was generated here will
### report "stored" (no OpenAI call) the next time the same text is sent -
### promoting a logged query into labelled_queries is CLI-only (`label`),
### never via this endpoint.

### Confident classification: a known test query, well ahead of the runner-up (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "How do I locate my card?" }

### Ambiguous classification: margin between rank 1 and 2 is under 0.02 (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "why did my cash get charged a fee that should not be there." }

### Normalization: different case/whitespace than the stored text still
### reuses its embedding - QueryText.Create collapses both to the same
### normalized text (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "  HOW DO I   locate MY card?  " }

### Request shape: "query" plus an optional "top" (default 3) for how many
### candidates come back. Representation is a CLI-only knob; the endpoint
### always classifies by centroid (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "where is the virtual card?", "top": 5 }

### 400: top below 1 (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "where is the virtual card?", "top": 0 }

### New query: not in the dataset, embedded on the fly (calls OpenAI).
### Sending this exact request again reports "stored" with no OpenAI
### call - it is now served from the query log.
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "the barista charged me twice for one iced latte" }

### Off-topic: nothing in Banking77 is close, so every candidate has low
### similarity (calls OpenAI)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "what's the weather like in Paris this weekend?" }

### 400: empty query (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "" }

### 400: whitespace-only query normalizes to empty (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "   \t  " }

### 400: over QueryText.MaxLength (1000 chars), rejected before any
### embedding call - 1001 "a"s below (no OpenAI call)
POST {{host}}/queries/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "" }
